version 0.10
view buck-5v

# TPS5430 5V/3A buck print page. Every net is drawn. GND is a bus below the parts (the view layer has
# no ground-symbol primitive); the divider's ground end sits above the parts, so it climbs to the bus
# through the gap left of C3. Different-net crossings are legal and carry no dot
# (spec/schematic-view.md §5.1): every dot on this page is a junction that exists.
#
# The buck is module M2 of the board, so the page names the board's flat ids: M2.U1, M2.C2, ...
# (spec/module.md §7). Every symbol origin and every bend below is a multiple of 0.5 mm (ADR-0057),
# so a pin point can always be reached by an axis-aligned run.
place
  M2.C1  117.5  96.5  90
  M2.C2  161.5  102.0  270
  M2.C3  211.0  106.5  90
  M2.C4  225.0  106.5  90
  M2.D1  177.5  108.5  90
  M2.L1  189.0  91.5  0
  M2.R1  197.0  103.0  90
  M2.R2  197.0  113.5  90
  M2.U1  140.0  105.0  0

